message: "Please cite DEEPBOM as: Kwon, J. (2026). DEEPBOM: Browser-Native Static Analysis of On-Device Neural Network Deployment Artifacts (Version 1.94.0) [Computer software]. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21834509"
title: "DEEPBOM: Browser-Native Static Analysis of On-Device Neural Network Deployment Artifacts"
type: software
version: 1.94.0
date-released: "2026-08-07"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21834509"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kwon"
    given-names: "Jun-Hwan"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6464-3895"
    affiliation: "Anesthesia and Pain Research Institute, Yonsei University College of Medicine"
    email: "kjh0442@yuhs.ac"
abstract: >-
  DEEPBOM is a browser-native static analyzer for deployment artifacts in
  TFLite, ONNX, GGUF, SafeTensors, and Core ML formats. It derives graph,
  tensor, quantization, memory, execution-provider, XNNPACK delegation, and
  target-fit evidence where the serialized contract and source-pinned rules
  permit deterministic assessment. Runtime-dependent claims remain explicitly
  separated from observed and derived static evidence. Model bytes and weights
  remain in the user's browser during analysis. This citation record preserves
  release identity and provenance for the hosted software. Repository contents
  and release artifacts remain governed by the license included with each
  version.
url: "https://deepbom.org/"
